design:
## Problem

We need:
1. ONE true Crate Cat that defines the character
2. Variants/adaptations that all trace back to that source
3. Flows that always seed with the canonical reference
4. Style consistency across all generations

## Asset Hierarchy

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                  CANONICAL REFERENCE                     │
│                                                          │
│  The ONE source of truth. Uploaded by user.             │
│  Never auto-generated. Sacred.                          │
│                                                          │
│  Example: crate-cat-canonical.png                       │
│  - The definitive Crate Cat look                        │
│  - Style, proportions, personality                      │
│  - Used as reference for ALL derived assets             │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                          │
                          ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                   STYLE VARIANTS                         │
│                                                          │
│  Pre-made adaptations of canonical for contexts.        │
│  Human-curated or carefully generated.                  │
│                                                          │
│  Examples:                                               │
│  - crate-cat-line-art.svg (for overlays)               │
│  - crate-cat-silhouette.svg (for any palette)          │
│  - crate-cat-warm-palette.png (warm album contexts)    │
│  - crate-cat-cool-palette.png (cool album contexts)    │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                          │
                          ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                 GENERATED INSTANCES                      │
│                                                          │
│  Per-album adaptations created by AI.                   │
│  Always reference canonical + context.                  │
│                                                          │
│  Examples:                                               │
│  - crate-cat-for-king-stingray.png                     │
│  - crate-cat-jazz-style.png                            │
│  - crate-cat-80s-neon.png                              │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## Schema

```typescript
// Asset with lineage tracking
const Asset = Schema.Struct({
  id: Schema.String,
  name: Schema.String,
  description: Schema.String,

  // Hierarchy
  assetType: Schema.Literal(
    "canonical",    // Source of truth, user-uploaded
    "variant",      // Pre-made adaptation of canonical
    "generated"     // AI-generated instance
  ),

  // Lineage - traces back to canonical
  canonicalRef: Schema.optional(Schema.String), // ID of canonical asset
  variantOf: Schema.optional(Schema.String),    // ID of variant (if generated from variant)

  // For canonical assets
  isCanonical: Schema.Boolean,
  canonicalFor: Schema.optional(Schema.Literal(
    "mascot",       // THE Crate Cat
    "setting",      // Reference photo for a setting
    "typography",   // Reference type specimen
    "texture"       // Reference texture
  )),

  // Style descriptors (extracted or defined)
  style: Schema.optional(Schema.Struct({
    palette: Schema.Array(Schema.String),
    lineWeight: Schema.optional(Schema.Literal("thin", "medium", "thick")),
    renderStyle: Schema.optional(Schema.Literal("line", "filled", "shaded", "realistic")),
    mood: Schema.optional(Schema.String),
  })),

  // Storage
  gcsPath: Schema.String,
  thumbnailPath: Schema.optional(Schema.String),

  // Generation metadata (for generated assets)
  generationContext: Schema.optional(Schema.Struct({
    prompt: Schema.String,
    model: Schema.String,
    referenceAssets: Schema.Array(Schema.String), // IDs used as reference
    albumContext: Schema.optional(AlbumContext),
  })),

  // Metadata
  createdAt: Schema.Date,
  createdBy: Schema.Literal("user", "agent", "system"),
});

// Canonical reference definition
const CanonicalReference = Schema.Struct({
  id: Schema.String,
  name: Schema.String, // e.g., "Crate Cat"
  description: Schema.String,

  // The canonical asset
  canonicalAssetId: Schema.String,

  // Pre-approved variants
  variants: Schema.Array(Schema.Struct({
    id: Schema.String,
    name: Schema.String,
    useCase: Schema.String, // When to use this variant
  })),

  // Style guide for generations
  styleGuide: Schema.Struct({
    mustPreserve: Schema.Array(Schema.String), // ["ear shape", "tail curl", "expression"]
    canAdapt: Schema.Array(Schema.String),     // ["color", "texture", "pose"]
    neverChange: Schema.Array(Schema.String),  // ["proportions", "face structure"]
  }),

  // Prompt template for AI generation
  generationPromptTemplate: Schema.String,
});
```

